---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubscribeForm from '../components/SubscribeForm.astro';
import Recommendations from '../components/Recommendations.astro';
import { recommendations } from '../data/writing';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Subscribe to Intentionaut | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="How leaders set direction when AI does more of the building. Field-tested with the receipts: what shipped, what broke, and what it cost."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Newsletter</p>
      <h1>How leaders set direction when AI does more of the building.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I write about it in practice: what shipped, what broke, and what it
        cost. Field-tested with the receipts.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose subscribe-page">
      <p>
        I've spent 15+ years on both sides of the bridge between the people who
        build and the boards who fund: production AI taken from a handful of
        experiments to millions of customers at Sainsbury's, some of the
        earliest LLM products in European recruitment at StepStone, and Cazoo's
        founding team through hyper-growth to a $7B IPO. The technology keeps
        changing. The hard part never does.
      </p>

      <p>What you'll get:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>What shipped, what broke, and what it cost, from my own AI-built products</li>
        <li>Where a model got something wrong: a number, a quote, a decision, and how I caught it</li>
        <li>The tools I build to fix my own process, released open source as I go</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Five to fifteen minutes per issue. No hype, no model-launch fever. If it
        doesn't change a decision you make, it doesn't make the cut.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="subscribe-cta" aria-label="Subscribe">
      <SubscribeForm
        variant="full"
        source="subscribe-page"
        emailId="subscribe-email"
        buttonLabel="Get the letter"
      />
    </section>

    <p class="subscribe-ps">
      P.S. Subscribers will see early thinking from my book in progress with Matt
      LeMay.
    </p>

    <Recommendations items={recommendations} heading="Not sure yet? Start here." />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .subscribe-page ul {
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }
  /* The prose block's own padding-bottom is the section gap to the form.
     Drop the trailing paragraph margin so the two don't stack. */
  .subscribe-page > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .subscribe-page li {
    margin-block: var(--space-2);
  }
  .subscribe-cta {
    /* .prose already carries the section's bottom padding (matches every
       service page: prose → CTA with no extra top margin). */
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .subscribe-ps {
    max-width: 46ch;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }
</style>
